  "preconditions": [
    "Owned temporary inputs and independently constructed native domain/record fixtures. Native safe descriptor reads for files; explicit binary streams. Real built module and zipapp in isolated empty-PATH child processes."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Normalize the same declared draft fields through owned mappings, real JSON files, explicit binary stdin and actual field option token binding; compare canonical intent bytes and hashes.",
    "Verify all 24 regular draft field types, exact textual semantics, language canonicalization, detached values and preservation of input files; reject generated fields, specialized records, malformed JSON, conflicts and unsafe input paths.",
    "Feed equivalent normalized requirement fields into the existing constructor with an explicitly supplied fixed identity, actor and time; compare the resulting native authoring preview binding without writes or entropy allocation.",
    "Exercise actual built module/zipapp adapters with real binary process stdin and passive code-like field text. Do not infer a registered artifact writer or its stdout contract.",
    "Reject missing/null required fields for all regular types and native conditional requirements. Check exact composite option values, control-field rejection, conflicting sources, broken/closed binary streams, actual file replacement/growth/shrinkage and FIFOs without visible identities or project writes. Verify actual built distribution invalid stdin diagnostics.",
    "Connect equivalent mapping/file/stdin inputs to the actual native embedding writer, check stored draft fields and its versioned result without claiming an implemented CLI stdout surface."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "Schreibende Authoring-Befehle MÜSSEN strukturierte Eingaben sowohl über `--input <FILE>` als auch über `--input -` von stdin akzeptieren und bei `--format json` ausschließlich ein versioniertes Ergebnisobjekt auf stdout ausgeben.",
    "scope": "Shared artifact-create field inputs normalize options, files and explicit binary stdin into canonical intent for24regular types without input-layer writes or allocation. The native7.c.W embedding service now connects those inputs to locked identity allocation, complete supplied-target validation and real transaction publication for applicable types, with required unavailable semantic gates failing closed. Registered CLI/stdout, complete production project/history loading, other authoring commands, platform and release scope remain partial."
  },
